<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ghazi Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1795–1832</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Ghazi Mulla</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi">Ghazi</a> Muhammad was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avar</a> scholar of the Naqshbandi order who became the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagestan">Dagestan</a> around 1828–1829. He preached holy war and strict <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharia">sharia</a> against Russian rule and local customary law, raiding Russian forts and towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kizlyar">Kizlyar</a>. He was killed when Russian troops stormed his home village of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gimry">Gimry</a> in 1832.</p></div>
